  "english": "10. Monday [Bch - Monday]. Tone 4, Plagal [Dz / D2]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Ask of Repentance Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]: \"Who is awesome\" (Որ ահաւոր).\n\n16. Sunday [Kir - Sunday]. Tone 3, Plagal [Dz / G2]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The period of eating meat [non-fasting period] is three weeks. See the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nSeptember:\n\n6. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 1, Plagal [Ak / A2]. Fourth. Ask Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]: \"Ineffable\" (Անճառելի). Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 1, Plagal [Ak / A2]: \"He was risen\" (Յարուցեալ էրն). Eve of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\n\n7. Monday [Bch]. Tone 2 [Bz / B1]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Ask of Repentance Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]: \"The voice of the youths\" (Մանկանցն զձայն).\n\n8. Tuesday [Gsh - Tuesday]. Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]. Fast. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Virgin from Anna.\n\n13. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 1 [Az / A1]. Exaltation of the Cross [Khachverats]. See the intervening period until the tenth Sunday in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\n20. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]. Second. Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]: \"The hosts of angels\" (Հրեշտակացն դասք). Eve of the Holy Cross of Varag.\n\n21. Monday [Bch]. Tone 1 [Az / A1]. Fast. Mamas, etc. Ask Tone 1, Plagal [Ak / A2]: \"You who are exalted\" (Որ բարձրեալդ ես).\n\n23. Wednesday [Dsh - Wednesday]. Tone 2 [Bz / B1]. Fast. Ask of Repentance Tone 3 [Gdz / G1]: \"Blessed are You, Lord, and glorified\" (Օրհնեալ ես տէր եւ փառաւորեալ).\n\n27. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 4 [Dz / D1]. Third. Feast of the Cross of Varag. The period of eating meat is seven weeks. See according to the order in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nOctober:\n\n4. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]. Fourth. Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]: \"Your resurrection\" (Ըզքո յարութիւնդ).\n\n11. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 4 [Dz / D1]. Fifth. Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 4 [Dz / D1]: \"The Myrrh-bearing women\" (Իւղաբեր), and \"Today the resurrection\" (Այսօր յարութիւն), and \"By the sign of the Cross\" (Ի Խաչանիշ).\n\n18. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]. Sixth. Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]: \"Christ rose\" (Քրիստոս յարեաւ), and \"Morning\" (Առաւօտեան).\n\n25. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 2 [Bz / B1]. Seventh. Discovery of the Cross [Gyut Khach].\n\n27. Tuesday [Gsh]. Tone 3 [Gdz / G1]. Hyperichians, and Severianos, etc. Ask Tone 1, Plagal [Ak / A2]: \"Holy God\" (Սուրբ Աստուած).\n\n28. Wednesday [Dsh]. Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]. Ask Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]: \"God Most High\" (Աստուած բարձր).\n\n31. Saturday [Shb - Saturday]. Tone 1 [Az / A1]. All Saints, ancient and new, etc. See also the others in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place, until the Friday of the third week. And on the Saturday come here and celebrate these feasts which are after the octave.\n\n25. Saturday [Shb]. Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]. Anton, and Tryphon, Barsamas and Onuphrius the hermits. If the year-letter is 8 [Te / Թ] in a leap year, on this Saturday do not celebrate Anton, because it was celebrated under the first letter 9 [To / Թ] after the Theophany [Birth of Christ]; but on Saturday celebrate Theodosius; on Monday, Kyriakos; on Tuesday, Vahan; and on Thursday, Tryphon with their companions. But in ordinary years, as it is set, celebrate in this manner.\n\n26. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]. Fourth. Ask Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]: \"Who in the heavenly\" (Որ յերկնային). Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]: \"When they came\" (Յորժամ եկին), and \"The angel descended from heaven\" (Էջ հրեշտակն յերկնից).\n\n27. Monday [Bch]. Tone 1 [Az / A1]. Theodosius the King and the youths of Ephesus.\n\n28. Tuesday [Gsh]. Tone 1, Plagal [Ak / A2]. Kyriakos and his mother Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Ask Tone 4 [Gdz / D1]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord of hosts\" (Սուրբ ես տէր զօրութեանց).\n\n30. Thursday [Esh - Thursday]. Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugene the Virgin, etc. Ask Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]: \"To You, O God\" (Առ քեզ աստուած).\n\nAugust:\n\n1. Saturday [Shb]. Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]. Athanasius and Cyril, and Gregory the Theologian.\n\n2. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 4 [Dz / D1]. Fifth. Ask Tone 2, Plagal [Bk / B2]: \"Without beginning, God\" (Անսկիզբն աստուած). Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 4 [Dz / D1]: \"The women anticipating\" (Կանանցն կանխելով).\n\n3. Monday [Bsh - Monday]. Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]. Eugene, Macarius, etc. Ask Tone 4, Plagal [Dk / D2]: \"Who [the wondrous]\" (Որ զհրաշափառ).\n\n4. Tuesday [Gsh]. Tone 1 [Az / A1]. Andrew the General, and his army, etc.\n\n6. Thursday [Esh]. Tone 2 [Bz / B1]. Adrian and his wife Anatolia, etc. Ask Tone 4 [Dz / D1]: \"You, the righteous\" (Զքեզ արդար).\n\n8. Saturday [Shb]. Tone 3 [Gdz / G1]. The Holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\n\n9. Sunday [Kir]. Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]. Sixth. Ask Tone 3 [Gdz / G1]: \"We glorify You\" (Փառաւորեմք զքեզ). Evening Hymn [Hamb.] Tone 3, Plagal [Gk / G2]: \"By the divine tomb\" (Զաստուածային զգերեզմանաւն). Eve of the Fast of the Mother of God.",
